<p>Agape is genuinely present with the Beloved. The embodiment of the virtues of love in meaningful relationship. This is foundationally divergent from Eros. It is not an ideal, not a concept. It is an act and a series of acts over time. Something real. The Beloved is the end unto themselves, rather than the means. Eros cannot hold what Agape is. The partner, the Great Work, is not a placeholder for a generalized cosmic principle of ascension.</p>
<p>The power can be found within <em>eudamonia and autarkeia</em>, in other words: happily flourishingly self-sufficiently and finally, present and abundantly overflowing from within.</p>

<h2>IO <em>Babalon</em></h2>
<p>In <em>Existential Kink</em> terms that’s the whole method. You don’t transcend the specific desire or the specific object, you grok it. You give as a drink from a cup that overfloweth, nourishing your entire being.</p>
<p>The Truth is in the formula.</p>
<p class="formula">93 93/93</p>
<p class="heart-line">Love is the Law. Love Under Will.</p>

<blockquote class="pullquote">“love is what love does, not what love feels”<cite>bell hooks</cite></blockquote>

